<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	P6 "watchOS workout capture" task (plan §Platform parity). HealthKit
	access to log a workout via HKWorkoutSession/HKLiveWorkoutBuilder
	(Sources/EnchiridionWatchKit/WorkoutSessionController.swift) plus
	background delivery so an in-progress workout keeps recording if the
	watch's screen sleeps or the app is backgrounded mid-run.

	DELIBERATELY NO `com.apple.security.application-groups` HERE (unlike
	every other target's `.entitlements` file in this directory): a
	watchOS app runs on a physically separate device from its iPhone
	companion app — there is no shared filesystem container between them
	the simple way there is between an app and its own in-process
	extension (which is what the App Group entitlement is for — see
	EnchiridionMac.entitlements' comment). This target's own
	`LocalGraphStore` lives at its own on-device path
	(EnchiridionWatchKit/WatchLocalStoreLocation.swift), never the
	`group.dev.rawkode.enchiridion2` container the phone/widgets/share
	extensions share — see that file's header for the full reasoning.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.healthkit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.healthkit.background-delivery</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
